{
 "sheet": 1,
 "name": "STP08CP05MTR",
 "kind": "led_driver",
 "manufacturer": "STMicroelectronics",
 "title": "STP08CP05: 8-channel constant-current LED sink driver with serial shift register, 3 V to 5.5 V",
 "source": {
  "document": "DocID13524",
  "revision": "Rev 8, August 2018",
  "pages": 30
 },
 "summary": "An LED display driver with eight constant-current sink outputs, each rated to 20 V, behind an 8-bit serial-in shift register and an 8-bit storage latch. One resistor on R-EXT sets the current of all eight outputs, anywhere from 5 mA to 100 mA, and the OE input gates the outputs for brightness control from 0 % to 100 %. It runs from 3 V to 5.5 V so it takes logic straight from a 3.3 V microcontroller, clocks at up to 30 MHz in a cascade, and drops in for the STP8C/L596 in function and footprint. STP08CP05MTR is the SO-16 part on tape and reel.",
 "key_figures": [
