 "equations": [],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Data path",
   "page": 11,
   "text": "Serial data on SDI is clocked into an 8-bit shift register on each rising CLK edge; the bit leaving the last stage appears on SDO for the next device in a chain. With LE high the 8-bit data latch is transparent and follows the shift register; when LE goes low the latch keeps its contents. A latched H turns its output on."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Output enable and brightness",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "OE is active low. Low passes the latched pattern to the outputs; high turns all eight outputs off without disturbing the registers. OE adjusts LED brightness from 0 % to 100 %; the shortest OE pulse is 200 ns."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Setting the output current",
   "page": 14,
   "text": "A single resistor from R-EXT to ground programs the current of all eight sinks. Typical settings at 25 °C: 3.9 kΩ for 5 mA, 970 Ω to 963 Ω for 20 mA, 190 Ω to 192 Ω for 100 mA, and 124 Ω for 130 mA, the highest setting reached. The recommended output range is 5 mA to 100 mA."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Output headroom",
   "page": 15,
   "text": "Each sink needs a minimum voltage across it to hold its current: roughly 30 mV at 3 mA, 150 mV at 20 mA, 390 mV at 50 mA and 850 mV at 100 mA, nearly the same at VDD = 3 V and 5 V. The current accuracy figures of ±1.5 % between bits and ±3 % between ICs apply at an output voltage of 1.3 V or more. Each output withstands 20 V, so several LEDs can sit in series on one channel."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Protection",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "An under-voltage lock-out watches VDD. A thermal shutdown acts on the output enable: at about 170 °C it turns off the outputs only. ESD rating is 2.5 kV HBM and 200 V MM."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Input structures",
   "page": 9,
   "text": "Every logic input passes through a 1 kΩ series resistor into a CMOS buffer, with a diode to GND at the pin. OE has a 300 kΩ pull-up to VDD and LE a 200 kΩ pull-down to GND. CLK and SDI have no pull resistor. SDO is a CMOS push-pull stage with a diode to GND."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Logic levels",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Inputs switch at 0.7 VDD and 0.3 VDD, so with VDD at 3.3 V the part takes logic directly from a 3.3 V microcontroller. The clock may run to 30 MHz in cascade; CLK rise and fall times are limited to 5 µs."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Thermal and power",
   "page": 16,
   "text": "Allowed dissipation falls linearly to zero at 150 °C. At 25 °C it is 2.5 W for TSSOP16 exposed pad, 1.4 W for DIP-16, 1.0 W for SO-16 and 0.88 W for TSSOP16. The exposed pad gives about 2.5 times the heat dissipation of the plain TSSOP and has to be soldered to the PCB to do so. The GND pin carries up to 800 mA."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Compatibility",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Pin-for-pin and functionally compatible with the STP8C/L596."
  }
 ],
